    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "A collective term referring to live animals, particularly bovine animals, held as property or reared to serve as meat, or sources of milk, skin, wool, etc.  [Source: Getty AAT] | hard, brittle internal structure found in all members of the family Sepiidae [Source: Wikidata] | the internal shell of the cuttle-fish, a light, cellular, calcareous body of an elongated oval form enclosed in the substance of the mantle; formerly used in medicine as an antacid and absorbent (OED s.v. cuttle-bone)" ;
